  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform conducting wire of length is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is wound up as a current carrying coil in the shape of an equilateral triangle of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and then in the form of a square of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>.&nbsp;The coil is connected to a voltage source <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The ratio of magnetic moment of the coils in case of equilateral triangle to that for square is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mi>y</mi></msqrt></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> is ____________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c969bdff-a96e-4b57-b431-604ca791f761-image.png\" style=\"width: 238px; height: 249px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>thus&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;turns</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/84e440e8-6a4e-4e03-8f5e-fd53b4fb6f7b-image.png\" style=\"width: 334px; height: 212px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msub><mo>an</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;turns</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>y</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>",
